WEBVTT

00:13.070 --> 00:15.870
Wow, what an amazing fight!

00:16.140 --> 00:18.580
A kaiju showdown! Freakin' awesome!

00:18.580 --> 00:21.000
Go! Levia!

00:21.000 --> 00:24.670
Setsu! Stop spectating and help!

01:59.550 --> 02:04.010
<b><i>Episode 3</i></b>

01:59.550 --> 02:04.010
<b><i>Frying a Squid for a Second Time</i></b>

02:04.380 --> 02:06.460
So, to reintroduce you...

02:06.460 --> 02:10.250
This is Levia, the god of the 
ocean and a friend of mine.

02:11.550 --> 02:14.850
You're most fortunate to even
have the opportunity to see me.

02:15.600 --> 02:16.940
You may thank me.

02:17.600 --> 02:21.330
Y-You're really the legendary 
god of the ocean?

02:21.900 --> 02:24.620
Wow, amazing...

02:27.170 --> 02:30.180
Hey, Setsu! Why didn't you help me?!

02:30.180 --> 02:31.880
Look at all this!

02:32.150 --> 02:36.000
Well, I assumed you'd be all right on your own.

02:36.000 --> 02:39.220
And I don't get many chances to see an awesome kaiju battle like that.

02:39.220 --> 02:41.710
You call me up suddenly after five years,

02:41.710 --> 02:44.740
make me ferry you over to the 
demonic continent, and then that?!

02:44.740 --> 02:46.370
That's pretty terrible!

02:48.430 --> 02:50.480
But, um...

02:51.020 --> 02:52.940
What are we going to do with this?

02:54.180 --> 02:56.940
We can't just leave it here...

02:59.000 --> 03:01.530
We can just let Setsu deal with it.

03:01.530 --> 03:03.280
Huh?! Me?

03:03.970 --> 03:05.350
<b>Squid Ring</b>

03:15.620 --> 03:19.230
Wh-What is this?! It's delicious!

03:19.920 --> 03:23.570
I haven't had Setsu's deep-fried squid 
in a while, but it's not bad.

03:23.570 --> 03:26.100
I prefer raw, though.

03:27.720 --> 03:30.680
Anyway, we've arrived at the demonic 
continent safely, for now.

03:31.100 --> 03:32.340
Yeah.

03:32.340 --> 03:36.080
The demonic fishing village 
of Volsee is close.

03:36.080 --> 03:40.280
And on the other side of that mountain 
is Evilbarrow, the Demon Lord's castle.

03:41.690 --> 03:43.330
The Demon Lord's castle?

03:44.970 --> 03:47.980
Yeah. That's where your package 
is supposed to go, right?

03:47.980 --> 03:50.430
I have business with its recipient, as well.

03:50.430 --> 03:53.410
A package, from a human to Dezas?

03:53.410 --> 03:56.630
Oh, yeah, she mentioned sending 
the brooch out for repairs.

03:56.920 --> 04:01.470
Huh? Levia-sama, do you know this 
Dezastol Serreno person, as well?

04:03.480 --> 04:06.890
Wait, does she not know who Dezas is?

04:07.270 --> 04:08.960
Seems not.

04:10.660 --> 04:14.590
The destination of your package is 
the Demon Lord's castle, Evilbarrow,

04:14.590 --> 04:17.360
and the recipient is Demon Lord Dezastol.

04:17.860 --> 04:18.540
Wha—

04:19.480 --> 04:21.390
What?!

04:21.390 --> 04:25.860
D-Dezastol is the Demon Lord?!

04:29.420 --> 04:32.380
Anyway, it's all on foot from here,

04:32.380 --> 04:35.860
so my job is done. Nice working with you.

04:36.670 --> 04:38.170
Aren't you coming with me?

04:38.510 --> 04:39.340
Why would I?

04:39.630 --> 04:41.430
What do you mean, why?

04:41.430 --> 04:46.180
It's been a while, and you know Dezas, so...

04:49.370 --> 04:53.660
I kept my promise and 
maintained peace on the seas.

04:53.660 --> 04:57.680
Then, five years later, you finally return,
 only to treat me like a boat!

04:57.680 --> 05:00.030
You're even hanging out with another woman,

05:00.030 --> 05:01.820
and that's what you say to me?

05:01.820 --> 05:04.990
Well, that's... I mean...

05:04.990 --> 05:07.700
A lot happened. I couldn't help it.

05:11.540 --> 05:13.800
Is this a lovers' quarrel?

05:13.800 --> 05:17.570
No matter what, the man has to 
apologize. Don't you know that?

05:17.570 --> 05:21.420
It seems like this guy doesn't 
understand girls' feelings at all.

05:21.940 --> 05:23.860
Say you're sorry.

05:27.060 --> 05:30.240
Here, have some squid rings and go away!

05:31.060 --> 05:32.070
What is this?

05:32.070 --> 05:33.180
Yummy!

05:33.180 --> 05:34.850
Squid rings are awesome!

05:34.850 --> 05:36.720
How is it so crunchy and fluffy?!

05:36.720 --> 05:40.450
Make some for Mom and Dad!

05:40.450 --> 05:44.400
You came at the right time. 
There's plenty more kraken left over.

05:44.700 --> 05:45.990
Yay!

05:47.660 --> 05:50.200
We can't just let it rot here!

05:50.810 --> 05:56.160
Pretty lady, thanks for 
making up for the no-good man!

05:56.670 --> 06:07.440
Squid rings! Squid rings!

06:07.930 --> 06:11.100
Damn that squid monster!

06:11.370 --> 06:14.040
We can't go fishing as long 
as that thing's out there.

06:14.040 --> 06:18.210
Not to mention, the merchants stopped
 coming here because of the war.

06:18.210 --> 06:21.190
At this rate, we'll run 
out of stored dried food.

06:22.210 --> 06:25.860
We don't have a choice. The whole 
village needs to fight that squid!

06:26.280 --> 06:27.990
Um, excuse me.

06:28.270 --> 06:31.960
Can I leave my squid here? 
We'll be eating it right away.

06:33.660 --> 06:36.910
The squid monster came back as food?!

06:49.920 --> 06:52.450
Praise Levia, god of the ocean! Hurray!

06:52.450 --> 06:55.350
Hurray! Hurray! Hurray!

06:55.350 --> 06:59.830
This is our village's finest 
drink. Please enjoy.

06:59.830 --> 07:01.740
Very nice, thank you.

07:05.500 --> 07:08.570
This is our signature seafood dish.

07:08.570 --> 07:10.300
It pairs well with the drink.

07:11.780 --> 07:15.410
Not bad... but isn't fish better eaten raw?

07:15.410 --> 07:17.540
This is as raw as it gets...

07:19.130 --> 07:23.790
Here, here! Squid rings from fresh kraken,
 caught just this afternoon!

07:24.160 --> 07:26.680
They're the best!

07:28.000 --> 07:31.470
Setsu! Too slow!

07:31.970 --> 07:35.300
Shut up! Don't make me do all the work!

07:44.100 --> 07:47.020
The kraken got sliced up into 
little rings straight away?!

07:47.020 --> 07:48.650
What skill!

07:48.650 --> 07:49.630
Yay!

07:49.630 --> 07:51.650
Awesome!

07:50.390 --> 07:51.650
Squid rings!

07:52.180 --> 07:53.780
Take it out, Ruri!

07:53.780 --> 07:54.570
Yes, sir!

07:54.570 --> 07:56.410
Taking it!

07:56.920 --> 07:59.060
Ruri, next batch coming up!

07:59.060 --> 08:00.540
Yes, sir!

08:00.540 --> 08:02.240
Ruri, hurry up!

08:02.240 --> 08:04.120
Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

08:07.250 --> 08:08.130
What?!

08:08.930 --> 08:10.860
The village is on fire?

08:10.860 --> 08:14.050
Have the humans landed on our shores?!

08:14.350 --> 08:18.510
As the head of Demon Lord Dezastol's
 personal guard, I, Vlad...

08:18.510 --> 08:21.020
will not let this stand!

08:21.020 --> 08:23.730
Just you wait, human soldiers!

08:31.410 --> 08:35.240
Oh, hey, Levia-sama!

08:36.060 --> 08:38.740
Good work out there!

08:39.490 --> 08:42.460
Hey, are you drunk, too?

08:42.460 --> 08:45.040
No, I'm not.

08:45.490 --> 08:47.730
Yeah, this is just juice.

08:47.730 --> 08:50.670
I told you so!

08:52.210 --> 08:56.300
Anyway, come on, Levia-sama. Let's chat.

09:00.360 --> 09:05.870
Levia-sama, how do you know Setsu-san?

09:05.870 --> 09:10.330
You two seem to know the 
Demon Lord very well, too.

09:14.000 --> 09:15.070
Let's see...

09:16.700 --> 09:19.080
If you phrase it like that,

09:19.820 --> 09:22.190
what's the right answer?

09:23.530 --> 09:27.800
Five years ago, Setsu tried to blaze 
across my ocean without permission.

09:27.800 --> 09:30.670
I fought him, and then,

09:30.670 --> 09:35.720
he demanded I help him finish 
the war and dragged me around.

09:35.720 --> 09:37.430
That was how it started.

09:40.730 --> 09:42.350
<i>In reality...</i>

09:42.470 --> 09:46.000
<i>All the noise of war had me so annoyed 
 that I went on a rampage,</i>

09:46.000 --> 09:48.790
<i>and he silenced me with one punch...</i>

09:50.620 --> 09:53.090
<i>But hey, technically I didn't lie, at least.</i>

09:54.010 --> 09:58.670
So that's how you met the Demon Lord. I see.

09:59.990 --> 10:03.920
I thought Setsu the Hero 
was famous in Distinia.

10:03.920 --> 10:04.910
Huh?

10:04.910 --> 10:13.510
Setsu the Hero? The person who got all 
the kings to be friends and end the war?

10:13.510 --> 10:14.840
That was...

10:14.840 --> 10:16.230
What?!

10:16.690 --> 10:20.640
Setsu-san is <i>the</i> Setsu?!

10:20.640 --> 10:27.890
That explains how he knows Levia-sama 
and the Demon Lord, and how he's so strong,

10:27.890 --> 10:32.650
but why would someone 
like that be my guard?!

10:33.390 --> 10:38.150
I guess Setsu wouldn't talk about 
his past without being prompted.

10:38.150 --> 10:43.220
S-So the number of accidents in the 
ocean suddenly dropping... That was...

10:43.220 --> 10:48.340
Yes. I promised Setsu that I'd 
maintain peace on the oceans.

10:48.340 --> 10:49.360
Yet...

10:50.510 --> 10:56.040
He suddenly disappeared, then reappears five 
years later and treats me like a boat!

10:57.690 --> 10:59.340
Don't you think that's pretty awful?

11:00.730 --> 11:05.060
Levia-sama, are you mad at Setsu-san?

11:06.860 --> 11:09.760
Well, I did get to see him again, 
so I guess it's okay.

11:11.020 --> 11:15.370
All right! Half off! It's a total steal!

11:12.820 --> 11:15.370
Half off? That's a good deal.

11:15.370 --> 11:16.490
Thanks!

11:15.370 --> 11:17.480
Wow, it's so much cheaper!

11:16.490 --> 11:19.200
Hey, don't push! Get in line!

11:17.480 --> 11:19.200
How much?

11:19.200 --> 11:21.860
You must really love Setsu-san!

11:23.680 --> 11:25.300
No way!

11:25.300 --> 11:27.830
The god of the ocean,
 in love with a human? No way.

11:29.400 --> 11:32.340
But I will admit, 
I was waiting for him to return.

11:35.500 --> 11:37.210
Everyone, are you all right?!

11:37.750 --> 11:40.730
I, Vlad, head of the Demon Lord's 
personal guard, am here!

11:40.730 --> 11:43.180
Humans, you won't get your way!

11:43.530 --> 11:44.590
Huh?

11:47.700 --> 11:49.430
What's wrong, mister?

11:53.230 --> 11:55.440
Want some squid rings?

11:56.400 --> 11:58.910
Squid... rings?

12:03.240 --> 12:06.200
<b>Sold Out</b>

12:39.250 --> 12:41.670
They really are best when they're raw.

12:41.670 --> 12:43.280
Levia-sama.

12:43.940 --> 12:46.160
Again, apologies for my behavior earlier.

12:46.610 --> 12:51.660
But I'm surprised that you're 
in town in your human form.

12:52.610 --> 12:54.750
Hey, Vlad, it's you.

12:55.280 --> 12:59.010
That sword, that magic power, 
and the squid rings!

12:59.010 --> 13:00.780
I knew it was you, Setsu.

13:00.780 --> 13:03.880
Though it was hard to tell, 
given your new form.

13:03.880 --> 13:05.430
Yeah, a lot happened.

13:05.800 --> 13:09.450
Anyway, seeing you, 
the Demon Lord's closest officer,

13:09.450 --> 13:11.880
out of the castle at a time like this...

13:11.880 --> 13:13.430
Is it because of the war?

13:13.910 --> 13:17.120
Yes. I was looking for Levia-sama.

13:17.580 --> 13:21.520
I didn't expect her to be with Setsu, 
the missing hero, though.

13:22.290 --> 13:24.570
I'm starting to see a ray of hope!

13:28.320 --> 13:30.580
Levia-sama and Setsu!

13:31.280 --> 13:34.620
I, Vlad, swallow my pride to implore you!

13:34.620 --> 13:37.750
Please, save the Demon Lord!

13:41.920 --> 13:49.010
The Demon Lord is being asked to 
marry a man named Terran Sneeter.

13:49.430 --> 13:54.310
Marriage? I don't know who that man is,
 but isn't that good news?

13:54.310 --> 13:56.840
It's not good at all!

13:56.840 --> 13:59.000
It's being called a marriage,

13:59.000 --> 14:01.680
but in reality, it's subjugation
 through a curse.

14:01.680 --> 14:03.560
A subjugation curse?

14:03.560 --> 14:06.600
But Dezas should be able 
to shrug off most curses.

14:06.600 --> 14:14.160
Well, he brought a powerfully cursed 
necklace instead of a ring.

14:14.940 --> 14:18.450
A curse so powerful that not 
even Dezas can resist it...

14:18.450 --> 14:22.720
You know of the war that 
started about a month ago,

14:22.720 --> 14:26.660
when the humans invaded us, right?

14:26.660 --> 14:29.480
What? The humans invaded?

14:29.480 --> 14:30.900
You didn't know?

14:30.900 --> 14:35.080
One of the coastal villages was 
attacked by soldiers in massive armor.

14:36.320 --> 14:39.260
They even left the flag 
of their country behind.

14:39.260 --> 14:41.520
A flag? Of Distinia?

14:42.330 --> 14:44.540
We were somehow able to fend them off,

14:44.540 --> 14:46.920
but they've attacked 
several more times since.

14:47.680 --> 14:51.690
The demon lord sent an emissary to the 
human nation, but they haven't returned.

14:53.070 --> 14:56.530
Taking advantage of the Demon 
Lord's reluctance to go to war,

14:56.530 --> 14:58.810
one man offered to negotiate.

14:58.810 --> 15:01.330
That man was Terran Sneeter.

15:01.650 --> 15:05.220
Oh? So that guy claims he can stop the war?

15:05.220 --> 15:06.340
He does.

15:07.610 --> 15:10.510
Is he really that powerful?

15:10.510 --> 15:12.680
Sounds kinda shady, to be honest.

15:12.680 --> 15:16.510
In a way, he's at the top of 
this world, like you are.

15:18.080 --> 15:24.360
Um, Setsu-san, he doesn't mean 
Terran himself is a strong fighter.

15:24.360 --> 15:27.390
Terran Sneeter is the world's 
wealthiest merchant,

15:27.390 --> 15:29.540
and head of the Terran Trading Company.

15:29.540 --> 15:33.380
Most of the merchant ships at sea are 
owned by the Terran Trading Company.

15:34.020 --> 15:38.750
Ah, right, those boorish ships 
that are all over the sea.

15:38.750 --> 15:42.700
He has a grip on all of the 
money and wealth in the world.

15:42.700 --> 15:49.230
Both we and the humans need the merchants' 
help to wage a cross-continent war.

15:50.160 --> 15:55.270
That's why we believe his claims 
aren't completely baseless, but...

15:55.270 --> 16:02.440
So Dezas is willing to become a slave, 
just to stop this war?

16:03.290 --> 16:04.770
Yes.

16:04.770 --> 16:09.290
What about you?! Are the generals of 
the Demon Lord's army okay with that?!

16:10.040 --> 16:15.250
Of course not! We will fight for the 
Demon Lord until the last man standing!

16:15.250 --> 16:16.370
Then why—

16:16.370 --> 16:20.420
Because she promised you
 she'd maintain the peace.

16:23.970 --> 16:29.760
What a silly woman, clinging to a promise 
she made with someone who disappeared.

16:30.200 --> 16:31.970
But that's precisely why...

16:34.680 --> 16:36.140
we can't leave her alone.

16:37.720 --> 16:38.720
Yeah.

16:40.010 --> 16:41.500
You're right.

16:55.430 --> 16:56.200
Let's go!

17:07.750 --> 17:09.520
Never thought we'd be using the same route

17:09.520 --> 17:12.850
we used to launch our surprise attack on the Demon Lord's castle back then.

17:12.850 --> 17:16.000
Yes, this brings back memories.

17:19.540 --> 17:21.810
Here's our welcoming party.

17:21.810 --> 17:26.730
Well, then, you can rely on 
me to serve as your escort!

17:28.400 --> 17:31.340
The date of the wedding ceremony 
that Terran mentioned is unclear,

17:31.340 --> 17:34.380
but given what the Demon 
Lord herself wants to do,

17:34.380 --> 17:36.600
we don't have a moment to waste.

17:36.600 --> 17:40.580
She was never one to back down 
once she'd made up her mind.

17:40.900 --> 17:45.180
Also, Terran is surrounded by skilled guards.

17:45.180 --> 17:47.990
The road to the castle is 
also crawling with monsters.

17:47.990 --> 17:51.090
Do try to conserve your magic power, Setsu.

17:51.630 --> 17:53.710
You can leave that part to me.

17:54.200 --> 17:57.010
Your words are truly reassuring. Thank you.

17:57.010 --> 18:00.300
I'm taking the shortest route. 
Can you keep up?

18:00.300 --> 18:03.740
Who do you think you're talking to? 
I'm the god of the ocean.

18:04.390 --> 18:06.680
Well, I'm off, then.

18:07.410 --> 18:10.230
I'll have it taken care of
 by the time you arrive.

18:17.060 --> 18:19.450
I'm counting on you, Setsu.

18:46.310 --> 18:48.240
So what's the plan?

18:48.240 --> 18:49.100
For what?

18:49.100 --> 18:51.050
When we get there.

18:51.050 --> 18:52.790
It's obvious.

18:53.680 --> 18:59.220
I'll blow away this stupid wedding or whatever, 
and that Terran guy along with it.

18:59.220 --> 19:03.910
But how will you stop the war 
without that rich merchant?

19:03.910 --> 19:07.410
I'm actually suspecting he's behind it.

19:09.570 --> 19:13.960
Vlad just said Distinia was the 
one that attacked first, right?

19:13.960 --> 19:18.670
But in Distinia, they said 
the demons attacked first.

19:19.680 --> 19:24.140
I also saw a bunch of big 
armored guys attack,

19:24.920 --> 19:28.680
but that wasn't Distinia <i>or</i> the demons.

19:29.000 --> 19:33.110
Look, this war didn't break out by 
pure coincidence like last time.

19:33.110 --> 19:34.870
Someone set it up.

19:36.110 --> 19:38.820
While both sides think 
they were attacked first,

19:38.820 --> 19:43.820
some shady dude comes in with 
a cursed necklace to sell peace.

19:44.720 --> 19:46.950
How much shadier can it get?

19:47.540 --> 19:49.580
So that Terran fellow is...

19:50.390 --> 19:53.640
I don't know who the true mastermind is,

19:53.640 --> 19:56.340
but I'm sure Terran at least knows something.

19:56.730 --> 19:58.590
In that case...

20:11.310 --> 20:13.440
I guess I don't need to hold back!

20:13.440 --> 20:17.600
Wow, you're a real beast on land, too.

20:17.600 --> 20:19.610
Did you actually get stronger?

20:19.950 --> 20:22.640
This is nothing compared to 
what I can do in the ocean.

20:22.640 --> 20:26.900
It's not like I was asleep 
the whole time you were gone.

20:32.870 --> 20:36.830
<i>Yes. It's always been like this with Setsu.</i>

20:36.830 --> 20:39.680
<i>We took risks, had adventures...</i>

20:43.950 --> 20:49.860
<i>Until five years ago, I had no interest 
in what happened on the shore.</i>

20:49.860 --> 20:55.010
<i>I just spent my time doing nothing 
at the bottom of the ocean.</i>

20:56.080 --> 21:01.360
<i>But after meeting Setsu, 
after being with him,</i>

21:01.740 --> 21:04.640
<i>I realized how beautiful this world is.</i>

21:04.640 --> 21:05.860
<i>That's why, right now...</i>

21:06.290 --> 21:10.260
<i>Not just because I promised Setsu, 
but also of my own free will,</i>

21:10.260 --> 21:12.400
<i>for these peaceful seas,</i>

21:12.400 --> 21:14.270
<i>this peaceful world...</i>

21:15.540 --> 21:18.970
I won't let Dezas take all the attention!

21:22.930 --> 21:26.260
Oh, yeah, one thing...

21:26.780 --> 21:28.140
What now?

21:28.400 --> 21:31.640
Your squid rings are better than raw squid!

21:33.020 --> 21:35.640
In that case, I'll make as many as you want.

21:40.190 --> 21:43.280
There it is! Evilbarrow, 
castle of the Demon Lord!

21:45.880 --> 21:47.780
Do your worst, Setsu!

21:48.290 --> 21:50.780
Yeah, count on it!

23:26.960 --> 23:31.970
<b><i>Next Time</i></b>

23:26.960 --> 23:31.970
<b><i>Receiving a Gift for a Second Time</i></b>

23:27.890 --> 23:31.000
Next time: "Receiving 
a Gift for a Second Time."
